      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T15:04:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve gotten mixed up with downstream using a choice symbol, while upstream has a single Kconfig symbol.\n\nBecause `CONFIG_TASK_HOSTCMD_THREAD_MODE` only has 2 settings, it can be converted to a single Kconfig bool, just like upstream.\n\nThe new downstream bool can then get guarded with `EC_HOST_CMD`, leaving the dependency managed by Kconfig instead of an #ifdef here.\n\nIf this makes sense, you could refactor `CONFIG_TASK_HOSTCMD_THREAD_MODE` as a separate CL.",
